From: kotwicha
Subject: [PATCH] Input: rmi4 - wait after the resume reset

psmouse switches off the PS/2 interface of an InterTouch device before
the SMBus side resumes, and a Synaptics sensor restarts from its
firmware defaults when that happens. rmi_smb_resume() programs it again
immediately. Some sensors, the TM3471 in AMD ThinkPads among them, have
been seen to report badly until their next reset after that: frames
come at an uneven rate, or the first frame of each touch is out of
date.

Sleep 300 ms between re-entering SMBus mode and rmi_reset().
---
diff --git a/drivers/input/rmi4/rmi_smbus.c b/drivers/input/rmi4/rmi_smbus.c
--- a/drivers/input/rmi4/rmi_smbus.c
+++ b/drivers/input/rmi4/rmi_smbus.c
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 #define SMB_MAX_COUNT			32
 #define RMI_SMB2_MAP_SIZE		8 /* 8 entry of 4 bytes each */
 #define RMI_SMB2_MAP_FLAGS_WE		0x01
+#define RMI_SMB_RESET_GRACE_MS		300
 
 struct mapping_table_entry {
 	__le16 rmiaddr;
@@ -384,6 +385,7 @@ static int rmi_smb_resume(struct device *dev)
 	int ret;
 
 	rmi_smb_reset(&rmi_smb->xport, 0);
+	msleep(RMI_SMB_RESET_GRACE_MS);
 
 	rmi_reset(rmi_dev);
 
